  "culturalNote": "The Maasai Mara is Kenya's most famous game park (mbuga ya wanyama), and \"safari\" is a Swahili word: it simply means \"journey\". Guides speak to each other in Swahili over the radio to share sightings. All animals take the same agreement as people, whatever their noun class: simba watatu (three lions), twiga ni mrefu (the giraffe is tall), tembo ni wakubwa (elephants are big).",
